WEBVTT

00:13.888 --> 00:18.351
Those who ceaselessly hone
their killing arts are known as "Masters."

00:18.727 --> 00:23.772
After many generations,
they have gained lethal abilities

00:23.773 --> 00:26.276
called "Modified Bloodlines."

00:26.943 --> 00:32.698
This is the story of one such Master,
the Poison Master, Hikaru Gero,

00:32.699 --> 00:35.243
and his attempts to get married.

00:43.752 --> 00:47.296
Locked in Latata

00:47.297 --> 00:50.966
Secrets in my veins Latata

00:50.967 --> 00:52.760
I know you want it

00:52.761 --> 00:54.553
And sure, I love it

00:54.554 --> 00:58.807
So I stay behind the mask Latata

00:58.808 --> 01:02.144
Run, run, run back to back Run

01:02.145 --> 01:06.023
Fun, fun, fun unpredictable but fun

01:06.024 --> 01:08.233
At the end of every mind game

01:08.234 --> 01:12.196
Shoot through the darkened night

01:12.197 --> 01:15.407
Poisoned in our bodies still

01:15.408 --> 01:20.079
Laugh at us our reckless souls

01:20.080 --> 01:21.413
TOXIC

01:21.414 --> 01:23.707
For you I will

01:23.708 --> 01:25.000
TOXIC

01:25.001 --> 01:27.419
Rewrite my destiny

01:27.420 --> 01:30.923
Losing it, falling for you

01:30.924 --> 01:34.384
What's tomorrow Kill or Kiss

01:34.385 --> 01:35.594
TOXIC

01:35.595 --> 01:37.930
Tell me what you want

01:37.931 --> 01:39.181
TOXIC

01:39.182 --> 01:41.475
I'll stay right here

01:41.476 --> 01:44.937
Like a spell, I'll be by your side

01:44.938 --> 01:48.608
What you gonna do Kill or Kiss

01:52.529 --> 01:55.115
Kill or Kiss

01:56.199 --> 01:58.660
Kill or Kiss

01:59.744 --> 02:01.996
Kill or Kiss

02:08.419 --> 02:10.129
Gero, Gero.

02:10.130 --> 02:14.007
Meet me tomorrow afternoon
at the Avocado Oceanic Art Gallery.

02:14.008 --> 02:15.259
A gallery on a ship?

02:15.260 --> 02:17.469
Wait, what happened to finding my charm?

02:17.470 --> 02:18.930
Don't sweat it. Just be there.

02:22.225 --> 02:23.976
Kinosaki's running late.

02:23.977 --> 02:25.811
Gero!

02:25.812 --> 02:27.564
Thanks for waiting!

02:31.025 --> 02:33.360
I took so long deciding
what to wear, I'm late.

02:33.361 --> 02:34.320
Come on. Let's go in.

02:36.447 --> 02:39.199
D-Don't you know it's rude
to touch someone out of the blue?

02:39.200 --> 02:41.034
What? Oh, come on.

02:41.035 --> 02:44.622
People burn through hundreds of thousands
of yen just to hold my hand.

02:52.630 --> 02:56.800
Anyway, this is what people
call a "date spot," right?

02:56.801 --> 02:58.218
Why bring me here?

02:58.219 --> 03:02.307
Today, you're going on your first date.
Or a rehearsal of it.

03:03.141 --> 03:07.060
Gero, even if you do manage to get
a woman's number and set up a date,

03:07.061 --> 03:09.521
you'll only crash and burn
the way you are now.

03:09.522 --> 03:11.566
Don't you want to go in prepared?

03:13.109 --> 03:15.069
What a cute doggy!

03:16.821 --> 03:18.823
Come on. Say something.

03:19.949 --> 03:21.825
A pretty shade of blue,
don't you think?

03:21.826 --> 03:24.494
Oh, well, I mean...

03:24.495 --> 03:27.205
Blue, uh... The sky is blue.

03:27.206 --> 03:30.418
You're too tense. Negative 10 points.

03:31.210 --> 03:33.587
This woman sure is gorgeous, isn't she?

03:33.588 --> 03:35.298
Y-You think so?

03:36.257 --> 03:38.800
Sh-She's not as beautiful as you.

03:38.801 --> 03:41.888
No one will buy that. Negative 100 points.

03:42.847 --> 03:44.599
What am I supposed to say?

03:45.558 --> 03:46.601
Gero.

03:47.060 --> 03:49.144
You don't have to try to impress me.

03:49.145 --> 03:50.021
But...

03:50.355 --> 03:52.732
A good date is one
where you both have fun.

03:55.318 --> 03:57.611
Easy for you to say.

03:57.612 --> 03:59.906
That's why we're practicing now.

04:00.573 --> 04:03.409
This is a thousand times harder
than my apprenticeship.

04:06.829 --> 04:08.580
I... I don't believe it.

04:08.581 --> 04:09.790
What's up?

04:09.791 --> 04:14.670
A 40-year-old DIY candy kit.
The first ever! Mixy-Mix Zero!

04:14.671 --> 04:16.213
It's valued at 30 million yen.

04:16.214 --> 04:17.339
Whoa, that price tag!

04:17.340 --> 04:20.008
That's too little.
I'd pay five times that amount.

04:20.009 --> 04:21.927
But it's just a cup and some powder.

04:21.928 --> 04:24.305
Its value doesn't lie in the materials.

04:25.306 --> 04:26.849
Okay, let's keep moving.

04:28.559 --> 04:31.646
You really do love those candy kits,
don't you, Gero?

04:35.066 --> 04:36.609
What is it this time?

04:37.360 --> 04:39.736
I just thought it looked neat
from this angle.

04:39.737 --> 04:40.655
Seriously?

04:43.908 --> 04:44.992
It really does.

04:44.993 --> 04:45.827
Right?

04:47.495 --> 04:50.539
Well, I guess I can give that 30 points.

04:50.540 --> 04:51.457
Harsh.

04:52.000 --> 04:54.419
It gives me hope for the future.

04:55.420 --> 04:57.212
Listen, Kinosaki.

04:57.213 --> 05:00.882
I appreciate the date rehearsal,
but don't keep me in the dark.

05:00.883 --> 05:02.802
What's my charm supposed to...

05:03.594 --> 05:04.971
Gero, look.

05:07.098 --> 05:09.309
What do you make of that guy?

05:09.767 --> 05:11.935
Well, I mean...

05:11.936 --> 05:13.604
- Sorry!
- Djungarian hamster.

05:14.230 --> 05:15.857
The restroom was crowded.

05:16.316 --> 05:17.441
Meerkat.

05:17.442 --> 05:19.151
That's his wife next to him.

05:19.152 --> 05:20.694
And that's not all.

05:20.695 --> 05:21.820
Mr. Shiratori?!

05:21.821 --> 05:22.946
Mr. Shiratori?

05:22.947 --> 05:25.033
Mr. Shiratori!

05:25.742 --> 05:29.119
He's the most popular painter
with young people right now:

05:29.120 --> 05:30.621
Takeru Shiratori.

05:30.913 --> 05:34.959
He may look and act like a weirdo,
but his fans wouldn't want it any other way.

05:35.335 --> 05:38.128
And all because he's a talented artist.

05:38.129 --> 05:39.297
Right.

05:39.589 --> 05:41.340
Take some other examples.

05:42.133 --> 05:44.760
A sportsman who always comes in clutch.

05:44.761 --> 05:46.094
Big Sis!

05:46.095 --> 05:48.723
A doctor who saves
a member of your family.

05:50.016 --> 05:53.144
A musician who punches a hole
in your boring, humdrum existence.

05:53.561 --> 05:56.605
They're liked for their talents

05:56.606 --> 06:01.318
in the same way looks and personality
draw folks to people they know,

06:01.319 --> 06:03.154
and those feelings are just as real.

06:04.072 --> 06:05.113
I see.

06:05.114 --> 06:07.240
So that's another kind of charm.

06:07.241 --> 06:08.366
But I don't-

06:08.367 --> 06:09.660
You do, Gero.

06:11.621 --> 06:14.040
Kinosaki, you don't need to do anything.

06:14.207 --> 06:16.500
Just close your eyes for 30 seconds.

06:16.501 --> 06:22.423
You took out a whole room full of bad guys
and rescued me all on your own.

06:24.217 --> 06:27.011
How could that not be part of your charm?

06:27.553 --> 06:29.971
So forget matchmaking parties and apps.

06:29.972 --> 06:33.810
What'll really let you shine
in your quest for a partner...

06:34.560 --> 06:35.978
is helping people.

06:37.522 --> 06:42.068
So rescue hostages and guard VIPs,

06:42.610 --> 06:45.404
and get them to fall for you
while you're at it.

06:45.780 --> 06:47.739
I know you can take on any job-

06:47.740 --> 06:51.244
S-Slow down. I'm a Poison Master.
I assassinate people.

06:51.577 --> 06:53.829
Nothing says you can't
save people, too, right?

06:53.830 --> 06:56.791
But I'd feel like I was
taking advantage.

06:58.126 --> 07:02.296
Listen. It really doesn't matter
how you get to know each other.

07:02.505 --> 07:04.714
Mr. Shiratori,
will you join us for dinner?

07:04.715 --> 07:06.050
We'd love you to!

07:06.217 --> 07:10.220
Whether you have ulterior motives or not,
it only gets you to the starting line.

07:10.221 --> 07:12.807
The real test is...

07:13.850 --> 07:17.227
whether you can build
a happy relationship after that.

07:17.228 --> 07:18.229
Mr. Shiratori?

07:18.604 --> 07:19.604
Mr. Shiratori?

07:19.605 --> 07:21.065
Mr. Shiratori?!

07:24.444 --> 07:27.988
Oh, Mr. Shiratori!
Can I get your autograph?

07:27.989 --> 07:28.989
Hey!

07:28.990 --> 07:30.867
Don't tell me that's why we're here.

07:32.702 --> 07:34.954
(My Girl, She's Like the Sun, Yeah?)

07:36.414 --> 07:38.708
Sir, we think it's the work of Himekawa.

07:39.584 --> 07:41.418
She won't get away with this.

07:41.419 --> 07:45.422
The captain bowed, scraped,
and poured blood, sweat, and tears

07:45.423 --> 07:48.717
into collecting these works
to make our visitors smile!

07:48.718 --> 07:50.427
Don't let her get away!

07:50.428 --> 07:53.805
Sink anything suspicious
that even comes near us!

07:53.806 --> 07:55.390
There's nothing on radar.

07:55.391 --> 07:58.059
Then, she must still be aboard.

07:58.060 --> 08:02.190
Get back My Girl, She's Like the Sun, Yeah?,
whatever it takes!

08:03.524 --> 08:04.232
Captain!

08:04.233 --> 08:07.487
My Girl, She's Like the Sun, Yeah?
has been stolen!

08:07.695 --> 08:09.238
It's a small price to pay.

08:14.368 --> 08:16.078
Thanks, Chompsky.

08:17.497 --> 08:19.790
Let's keep business out of our next date.

08:21.125 --> 08:22.667
Hey!

08:22.668 --> 08:24.754
Hey, guys! Sorry I took so long!

08:41.646 --> 08:44.773
Save girls when they're in a bind
and get them to fall for you.

08:44.774 --> 08:47.401
I call it Operation White Knight.

08:48.736 --> 08:50.278
What's with that look?

08:50.279 --> 08:53.157
Nothing. It's just...
I'm not much of a "knight."

08:54.033 --> 08:55.910
You can be a squire, then.

08:56.786 --> 08:59.664
Setting the name aside...

08:59.914 --> 09:03.543
The question is, how am I going
to find jobs rescuing people?

09:07.171 --> 09:08.339
Never mind.

09:08.673 --> 09:11.551
I shouldn't have asked
while you were eating.

09:12.552 --> 09:13.760
The Dark Nav?

09:13.761 --> 09:14.470
Yup.

09:14.887 --> 09:17.598
Murder. Smuggling. You name it.

09:17.890 --> 09:21.101
This site will hook you up
with all kinds of shady jobs.

09:21.102 --> 09:26.649
Finding rescue and bodyguard gigs
will be a cinch on the Dark Nav.

09:26.899 --> 09:28.608
You mean you've never used it?

09:28.609 --> 09:31.861
I've never even heard of it.
All our jobs go through a broker.

09:31.862 --> 09:36.200
Wow. Talk about traditional.
You old families sure do things differently.

09:36.993 --> 09:38.660
May I take your order?

09:38.661 --> 09:40.161
This one will eat for two.

09:40.162 --> 09:42.206
Five plates of marinated skirt steak!

09:47.920 --> 09:50.339
I'm drowning in meat juices!

09:50.590 --> 09:53.133
I only see scam and smuggling jobs.

09:53.134 --> 09:56.678
You could take your pick
if you had an account.

09:56.679 --> 09:59.098
Well, excuse me for being old-fashioned.

10:00.474 --> 10:01.601
Hey, Kinosaki.

10:01.851 --> 10:02.977
How about this one?

10:05.771 --> 10:10.151
Our demands are the artworks
you've taken temporary custody of.

10:10.318 --> 10:11.610
All of them.

10:11.611 --> 10:14.947
We'll tell you where to exchange them
for Himekawa later.

10:15.531 --> 10:21.328
The criminal underworld knows
Kyoko Himekawa as an infamous thief.

10:21.329 --> 10:26.625
But the truth is, malicious collectors
steal art from the disadvantaged,

10:26.626 --> 10:29.420
and she returns it all
to the original owners.

10:29.962 --> 10:35.384
Himekawa trusted us with these artworks.
We can't just hand them over!

10:35.718 --> 10:40.388
So we'd like you to infiltrate
their hideout before the exchange

10:40.389 --> 10:43.559
and rescue Himekawa for us!

10:47.772 --> 10:50.315
I knew we didn't offer
anywhere near enough money.

10:50.316 --> 10:52.859
But what can we do? We live gig to gig.

10:52.860 --> 10:54.861
I know! I'll sell all of my organs!

10:54.862 --> 10:56.696
Kitami, calm down.

10:56.697 --> 11:00.660
It makes sense no one would take
a risky job that pays so little.

11:00.951 --> 11:05.247
But with no competition to be her knight
in shining armor, this is Gero's chance.

11:05.706 --> 11:07.082
We're doomed!

11:07.083 --> 11:08.208
Excuse me.

11:08.209 --> 11:10.627
He's a Master from the Gero family.

11:10.628 --> 11:12.170
Hikaru Gero.

11:12.171 --> 11:15.132
I'm here to rescue your boss,
Kyoko Himekawa.

11:16.634 --> 11:19.844
Gero? You mean, the Poison Masters?

11:19.845 --> 11:22.639
Wh-What's a Master doing here?

11:22.640 --> 11:26.352
We'd need to sell all of our organs
just to cover the broker's fee!

11:26.769 --> 11:31.899
Still, with a Master on our side,
we'd rescue Himekawa, no problem!

11:33.109 --> 11:35.903
When you want to take a castle,
start with its outer defenses.

11:39.031 --> 11:43.202
Hey, you guys. I still have
an important question for you.

11:43.411 --> 11:44.702
Wh-What is it?

11:44.703 --> 11:46.288
He does want our organs.

11:47.665 --> 11:49.500
I assume Himekawa...

11:49.750 --> 11:51.627
doesn't mind men who wear glasses?

11:55.881 --> 11:58.008
(What Is "Charm," Anyway?)

12:00.261 --> 12:02.263
(No Unauthorized Personnel
Beyond This Point)

12:02.888 --> 12:07.810
I've never found anyone
as beautiful as I find you.

12:08.144 --> 12:10.937
I'll guarantee you a life
in the lap of luxury.

12:10.938 --> 12:13.983
What would you say to giving up
your petty thievery...

12:15.943 --> 12:18.529
and becoming part of my collection?

12:18.779 --> 12:20.239
No way in hell.

12:21.824 --> 12:25.286
I steal for what I believe in.

12:25.744 --> 12:26.954
They're crying.

12:27.663 --> 12:30.624
All those works of art you took
from their rightful owners.

12:31.333 --> 12:35.128
The late Egg Saturnia was a master
of the Suntanned Beauty School of Art.

12:35.129 --> 12:41.050
The stolen portrait, My Girl, She's Like
the Sun, Yeah?, is of his daughter.

12:41.051 --> 12:43.846
It has a market value in
the region of two billion yen.

12:44.805 --> 12:49.101
I heard about you from an art dealer.
He and Egg went way back.

12:49.727 --> 12:54.023
Please. It was the only painting
of my wife we'd hung on to.

12:54.482 --> 12:55.733
And for our daughter...

12:56.859 --> 12:57.943
Sorry...

12:58.486 --> 13:00.321
but I made that little girl a promise.

13:01.197 --> 13:04.450
Don't worry. I'll make sure
you get to see your mom again soon.

13:06.327 --> 13:09.205
I promised to steal her back.

13:09.580 --> 13:12.583
So don't cry.

13:17.880 --> 13:19.380
Ushio.

13:19.381 --> 13:23.010
Would you mind breaking her spirit for me?

13:24.053 --> 13:25.512
Seriously, Gero.

13:25.513 --> 13:28.181
You were taking a big risk
with that question.

13:28.182 --> 13:30.391
It threw them all for a loop.

13:30.392 --> 13:31.643
Men who wear glasses?

13:31.644 --> 13:33.186
Is it code for something?

13:33.187 --> 13:36.524
Letting them in on what you're after is
about as far from a knight as you can get.

13:38.108 --> 13:42.029
Either way, I took the job,
so I'll do it right.

13:44.198 --> 13:48.034
Man, I can't believe I'm making
another trip here with you.

13:48.035 --> 13:51.663
According to the freakishly accurate GPS
her assistant, Kitami, lent us,

13:51.664 --> 13:53.749
we should be almost there.

13:55.709 --> 13:56.961
Rats get exterminated.

13:57.294 --> 13:58.170
That's the rule.

14:11.809 --> 14:12.810
Kinosaki.

14:13.185 --> 14:14.895
Which way should we go now?

14:15.479 --> 14:19.483
Gero, I really think
I should sit this one out.

14:20.568 --> 14:22.278
I need you.

14:26.365 --> 14:30.995
I've never met this woman,
and I've got no clue how to talk to her.

14:31.829 --> 14:33.247
Oh, all right.

14:33.581 --> 14:35.040
Let's go over the basics.

14:43.132 --> 14:45.217
Stop, Ushio.

14:46.510 --> 14:48.721
Some rats have snuck aboard.

14:49.138 --> 14:50.723
Go mash 'em up.

14:53.434 --> 14:56.270
What? That all ya got?

14:56.854 --> 14:58.272
Now...

14:58.731 --> 15:01.025
Let's try something different.

15:02.276 --> 15:03.527
Hikaru Gero.

15:03.819 --> 15:05.153
Poison Master.

15:05.154 --> 15:07.197
W-Would you please...

15:07.781 --> 15:09.658
date me with the intent to marry?

15:09.783 --> 15:10.784
Don't you dare.

15:11.327 --> 15:13.662
If this were the real deal,
you just killed your chances.

15:14.038 --> 15:15.496
So what am I supposed to say?

15:15.497 --> 15:17.165
- Freeze!
- Or you're dead!

15:17.166 --> 15:19.208
Write this down later.

15:19.209 --> 15:24.172
The key to finding a partner is thinking
through how things make them feel.

15:24.173 --> 15:26.549
So forget marriage for now.

15:26.550 --> 15:28.051
Huh? You're not making se-

15:28.052 --> 15:30.179
She doesn't care about your problems!

15:31.180 --> 15:32.389
Stop right there!

15:32.640 --> 15:36.894
Gero, you're the Master
who came to rescue Kyoko Himekawa.

15:38.020 --> 15:42.232
She's trapped in this place.
She must feel numb with terror.

15:42.900 --> 15:44.526
What will you say to her?

15:47.029 --> 15:49.365
Okay, let's run through it again.

15:53.577 --> 15:57.665
A gun? After all that buildup?
Talk about a letdown.

15:57.957 --> 15:59.791
I'm sure you think so...

15:59.792 --> 16:01.126
when it's pointed at you.

16:01.835 --> 16:02.878
Hey, wait!

16:03.629 --> 16:06.047
I should've done this from the start.

16:06.048 --> 16:08.883
You're a collector.
You must know its worth.

16:08.884 --> 16:13.847
To add you to my collection,
it's a small price to pay.

16:14.348 --> 16:17.101
You will be mine now, won't you?

16:19.103 --> 16:24.316
I promised to bring that girl's mom back.
Now I'm putting her in danger.

16:25.776 --> 16:28.904
Fine. I'll do whatever you...

16:35.744 --> 16:39.748
My arm!

16:44.211 --> 16:47.715
What happened?! Who did that?!
This room is supposed to be secure!

16:52.553 --> 16:55.597
Thanks for giving me that makeover.

17:02.896 --> 17:04.273
Keep dreaming.

17:05.524 --> 17:08.193
I'm Hikaru Gero, Poison Master.

17:08.694 --> 17:10.404
I'm here to save you.

17:11.030 --> 17:12.406
You're safe now.

17:13.532 --> 17:17.618
It's as simple as it gets,
but it'll hopefully help cheer her up.

17:17.619 --> 17:19.913
A Master? Seriously?

17:20.497 --> 17:22.833
We don't have that kind of money.

17:24.543 --> 17:26.836
What'd they do? Sell their organs?

17:26.837 --> 17:29.923
Oh, right. We'd only planned out
his introduction.

17:30.257 --> 17:33.093
He jumped in before
we'd finished rehearsing.

17:33.969 --> 17:35.763
Oh, let me get those off you.

17:36.346 --> 17:39.516
But I'm glad. We got here
before the worst could happen.

17:48.400 --> 17:49.902
Kill those rats...

17:50.194 --> 17:52.404
Water Master Ushio.

18:01.205 --> 18:02.873
Take a nap like your boss.

18:04.374 --> 18:05.292
Water?

18:08.420 --> 18:09.378
So fast.

18:09.379 --> 18:10.129
Kinosaki!

18:10.130 --> 18:10.923
Take Himekawa!

18:13.467 --> 18:15.803
Gero, you need to treat girls delicately!

18:16.095 --> 18:18.305
Sorry! You can tell me all that later!

18:34.154 --> 18:35.447
Gero!

18:42.204 --> 18:44.915
Forgive me for not
introducing myself sooner.

18:45.207 --> 18:47.416
Here is my card.

18:47.417 --> 18:49.836
Poison Master Gero, I presume?

18:49.837 --> 18:51.547
What is she, a businesswoman?

18:51.922 --> 18:56.468
I realize this is sudden, but would you
consider settling this matter privately?

18:56.927 --> 19:01.515
A fight between Masters will result
in greater losses than your fee will cover.

19:01.932 --> 19:07.061
So allow me to offer you ten times
what your client is paying you.

19:07.062 --> 19:12.651
This is business. I know you'll set aside
loyalty, compassion, and trust.

19:13.110 --> 19:17.197
A businessman who sits down to dinner
with his family every night at six

19:17.614 --> 19:21.534
can never achieve exponential growth.

19:21.535 --> 19:22.869
What is she talking about?

19:22.870 --> 19:25.538
A professional should ignore
unnecessary distractions...

19:25.539 --> 19:28.374
Gero's steroid thing.
And there's still some left.

19:28.375 --> 19:29.584
I'd better grab it.

19:29.585 --> 19:30.210
Don't touch it!

19:33.005 --> 19:35.674
I see. That must be deadly poison.

19:37.426 --> 19:41.680
Masters pass down Modified Bloodlines
along with their calling.

19:41.972 --> 19:47.728
The Poison Masters' one strengthens you
in response to lethal doses of poison.

19:48.061 --> 19:52.065
You might call it a survival strategy
adapted to the world we Masters live in.

19:52.441 --> 19:54.359
Like hell it is.

19:54.610 --> 19:59.323
This curse forces us to finish off
our targets before we drop dead.

19:59.615 --> 20:03.869
If you're a Water Master, your weird tricks
must use a Modified Bloodline, too.

20:04.244 --> 20:06.788
Although they look like magic from here.

20:08.582 --> 20:13.669
As you say. And with all due respect,
neither poison needles nor poison gas

20:13.670 --> 20:16.380
can penetrate my company's
"business suit."

20:16.381 --> 20:19.759
Its airtight design can stand up
to extreme water pressure.

20:19.760 --> 20:22.304
Now, as for our settlement...

20:24.056 --> 20:27.351
I see. How deeply regrettable.

20:35.150 --> 20:35.984
I see.

20:36.443 --> 20:40.948
The Poison Masters' Modified Bloodline
makes you faster as you near death.

20:41.281 --> 20:42.782
That is a setback.

20:42.783 --> 20:45.284
One hit, and I'm out.

20:45.285 --> 20:51.040
The Gero Poison Masters are one of
the Five Great Families. Industry leaders.

20:51.041 --> 20:55.128
Wouldn't you rather engage
in more meaningful value creation?

20:56.296 --> 20:59.883
Or do you consider Himekawa
a lucrative client?

21:00.300 --> 21:01.677
Or maybe something more?

21:02.219 --> 21:04.638
Don't tell me you're
romantically involved?

21:10.727 --> 21:15.023
Not much of a counterattack.
You barely grazed me.

21:17.401 --> 21:18.944
The hell did he smear on-

21:21.905 --> 21:23.657
Himekawa and I...

21:23.949 --> 21:25.367
are complete strangers.

21:32.666 --> 21:33.583
But...

21:40.090 --> 21:42.801
She might mean a lot to me someday.

21:45.887 --> 21:49.850
He hit me three times in the same spot,
right down to the millimeter.

21:50.309 --> 21:54.730
I must say, I don't know
what you're babbling about.

21:55.230 --> 21:56.606
I bet not.

21:56.940 --> 21:59.901
From your perspective,
I'm a nonsensical moron.

22:00.527 --> 22:00.861
But...

22:02.112 --> 22:05.991
Remember sitting down to dinner
with family every night at six?

22:06.867 --> 22:10.120
That idea you dismissed as useless?

22:12.289 --> 22:13.790
That's the stuff I want.

22:14.333 --> 22:15.917
Even if it kills me.

22:28.680 --> 22:30.973
Ah! Something smells fishy!

22:30.974 --> 22:32.892
I'm shocked, startled,
it's adding insult to injury

22:32.893 --> 22:34.226
I'm completely obsessed

22:34.227 --> 22:36.604
Ah! Something smells off!

22:36.605 --> 22:38.606
You're all bluff,
I'm sick and tired, so disappointed

22:38.607 --> 22:39.649
Bye-bye, mwah!

22:39.941 --> 22:42.777
It seems like I'm only good at

22:42.778 --> 22:45.613
workbooks for a child

22:45.614 --> 22:48.365
Even through infectious disease,
I want to love with you

22:48.366 --> 22:51.327
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

22:51.328 --> 22:53.829
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:53.830 --> 22:57.041
Darling, heading toward a twisted signpost

22:57.042 --> 22:59.543
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:59.544 --> 23:02.297
Just the two of us, consolation prize

23:12.557 --> 23:14.767
Ah, the scent of dance

23:14.768 --> 23:16.602
I'm completely obsessed

23:16.603 --> 23:18.020
with you as you flutter down

23:18.021 --> 23:20.272
Ah, something smells off

23:20.273 --> 23:22.483
I'm blown away by you

23:22.484 --> 23:23.484
Bye-bye, mwah!

23:23.485 --> 23:26.612
It seems like I'm only good at

23:26.613 --> 23:29.365
workbooks for a child

23:29.366 --> 23:32.201
I want us to share even our growing pains

23:32.202 --> 23:34.871
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

23:35.080 --> 23:37.665
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:37.666 --> 23:40.751
Darling, heading toward
a stagnant signpost

23:40.752 --> 23:43.337
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:43.338 --> 23:46.091
Singing a grand chorus cheekily

23:48.009 --> 23:49.635
- I'll compensate you, of course.
- I love these.

23:49.636 --> 23:51.804
- Date Mission, start!
- Stealing my heart ain't easy.

23:51.805 --> 23:54.181
I want you to have
the best possible marriage.

23:54.182 --> 23:56.977
Next time: "My First."
